-- sandblaster prelude lemmas: the generic `Seq` library (pe P3, C1): `get`,
-- `skip` (`seq::drop`), `take`, `++` (`seq::append`), cons and indexing,
-- each against the others, and the `[init @ .., last]` view (`take_snoc`).
-- A `Nat` parameter's bound `0 ≤ n` is the binder after the parameters.
--
-- Checked, untrusted. Machine-written: each proof is the kernel term the
-- front end produced for the same statement proved in the DSL at an element
-- type `E`, generalized to the type parameter `T`
-- (sandblaster/front/tests/samples/p3_lemmas/seq.rs, generator
-- `gen.py` there; `prover_ergonomics_p3::p3_lemmas_match_their_source` checks
-- that the source still proves exactly these statements). `auto` uses them
-- as conditional rewrite rules, each tried only on goals that mention its
-- left side's head function (`auto::lemmas`, `auto::ematch`).

